#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "2de283b3-992c-588c-8bda-e880779fa264" :question/math-academy-id "e-5796" :question/problem "The Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x)$. Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/897/Source/Images/0dcad03e8bddad5bbf3557260060a9c4.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x_1=-2}$, ${x_2=3}$, and\n\n$$\n{x_{3,4}=1 \\pm 3\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=1}$. Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= a(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3})(x - x_{4}) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (x - (-2))(x - (3))(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= (x + 2)(x - 3)(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 2)(x - 3)(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x^{2} - 3x + 2x - 6)(x^{2} - x(1 - 3\\textrm{i}) - x(1 + 3\\textrm{i}) + (1 + 3\\textrm{i})(1 - 3\\textrm{i})) &=  \\\\\n(x^{2} - x - 6)(x^{2} - 2x + 10) &=  \\\\\nx^{4} - 2x^{3} + 10x^{2} - x^{3} + 2x^{2} - 10x - 6x^{2} + 12x - 60 &=  \\\\\n&= x^{4} - 3x^{3} + 6x^{2} + 2x - 60 \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 6x^2 + 2x - 60\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087587 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "3630f36c-b507-5540-bb11-aeda6aa4d656" :question/math-academy-id "e-8801" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=0, x_2=-1,x_3=2$ and $x_4=-3$, and the coefficient of the quartic term is $4$. Find $P(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{x_1=0, x_2=-1}\n$$\n\n${x_3=2}$, and ${x_4=-3}$, and the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=4}$, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3})(x - x_{4}) &= 4(x - 0)(x - (-1))(x - 2)(x - (-3)) \\\\\n&= 4(x - 0)(x + 1)(x - 2)(x + 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4(x - 0)(x + 1)(x - 2)(x + 3) &= 4(x^{2} + x)(x^{2} + x - 6) \\\\\n&= 4(x^{4} + x^{3} - 6x^{2} + x^{3} + x^{2} - 6x) \\\\\n&= 4(x^{4} + 2x^{3} - 5x^{2} - 6x) \\\\\n&= 4x^{4} + 8x^{3} - 20x^{2} - 24x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x) = 4x^4+8x^3-20x^2-24x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7df4e54-eb56-5909-9eac-4132f178cc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} - 3x^{3} - 12x - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087001} {:answer/id #uuid "d55caf15-5c98-5438-bb19-57d0c4e4f9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} - 3x^{3} + 10x^{2} - 2x - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087002} {:answer/id #uuid "0f50a137-98fe-5444-b7e3-1ecaf71c4e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} + 3x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 2x - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087003} {:answer/id #uuid "35049fed-867c-57a5-81d4-ffa314df0c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} + 10x^{2} - 2x - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087004} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7debf4-ad8d-5d41-a200-fa1737426947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} - 3x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/i